From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 13] amdgpu: PRIME exports to other devices on illumos

Another device maps amdgpu's (private, TTM) objects through the DRM
core's PRIME maps, which call the exporting driver back to pin an
object and hand out its pages. amdgpu_pci_probe() gives LinuxKPI those
callbacks (amdgpu_illumos_prime_init(), illumos/amdgpu_dma_buf_illumos.c)
as soon as the DRM device exists.

License: a preprocessor-guarded call in an MIT file; applied to the
pinned Linux tree.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -2374,6 +2374,11 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
+#ifdef __illumos__
+/* illumos/amdgpu_dma_buf_illumos.c */
+extern void amdgpu_illumos_prime_init(struct drm_device *ddev);
+#endif
+
 static int amdgpu_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 			    const struct pci_device_id *ent)
 {
@@ -2428,6 +2433,10 @@
 	adev->dev  = &pdev->dev;
 	adev->pdev = pdev;
 	ddev = adev_to_drm(adev);
+#ifdef __illumos__
+	/* Other devices map amdgpu's objects through the DRM core's PRIME. */
+	amdgpu_illumos_prime_init(ddev);
+#endif
 
 	if (!supports_atomic)
 		ddev->driver_features &= ~DRIVER_ATOMIC;
